let __v_2458 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"jam\",\"jams\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"marmalade\",\"marmalades\"]},\"Jam is fruit cooked with sugar until it sets, and it is soft enough to spread; marmalade is citrus - usually Seville oranges - cooked with sugar and shreds of peel, so it is firmer and has a bitter edge. Same method, different fruit: anything with peel shreds in it is marmalade.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"lake\",\"lakes\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"pond\",\"ponds\"]},\"Ponds are small and shallow: light reaches the bottom across most of one, so plants grow right through the middle. A lake is deep enough to have open water in the middle, with its own wind-driven ripples and a shore where plants stop. There is no exact size that splits them, but a pond you could wade across is a pond.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"wage\",\"wages\",\"hourly pay\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"salary\",\"salaries\",\"yearly pay\"]},\"A wage is paid for the hours you worked, so overtime adds and a short week takes away; a salary is one yearly figure paid in twelve equal months whatever the hours. Hourly pay is better when you work extra, a salary is steadier when work is quiet.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tortoise\",\"tortoises\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"turtle\",\"turtles\",\"terrapin\",\"terrapins\"]},\"Tortoises live on land: domed shell, stumpy elephant-like back legs, and they cannot swim. Turtles live in water: a flatter, streamlined shell and flippers, and the sea turtles only come ashore to lay. A terrapin is the small freshwater turtle people keep in a pond.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"frog\",\"frogs\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"toad\",\"toads\"]},\"A frog has smooth, damp skin, long back legs and jumps; a toad has dry, warty skin, shorter legs and walks or makes small hops. Frogs stay near water and toads wander further from it, coming back only to breed, and toads lay their eggs in strings rather than clumps.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"baking powder\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"bicarbonate of soda\",\"bicarb\",\"bicarbonate\",\"baking soda\"]},\"Bicarbonate of soda is an alkali on its own: it only fizzes when it meets an acid such as buttermilk, lemon or vinegar. Baking powder is bicarbonate with that acid and a little starch already mixed in, so it raises on its own - which is why a recipe can call for three times as much baking powder as it would bicarb, and why swapping one for the other flatly does not work.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"stock\",\"stocks\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"broth\",\"broths\"]},\"Stock is bones and scraps simmered for hours, and it sets to a jelly when cold because of the gelatine; it is an ingredient, not a dish. Broth is usually simmered for an hour or two with meat and vegetables still in it and is eaten as it is. Same pot, different job.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"stew\",\"stews\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"casserole\",\"casseroles\"]},\"A stew is meat and vegetables cooked slowly in liquid on top of the hob; a casserole is the same food cooked in a covered dish in the oven. The dish gives the name, not the recipe, so a casserole is a stew in a lidded pot.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"muffin\",\"muffins\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"cupcake\",\"cupcakes\"]},\"A cupcake is a small cake - butter, sugar, eggs, flour - baked in a paper case and iced. In Britain a muffin is a flat, round yeast bread, split and toasted; in America a muffin is a soft, barely sweet quick bread with no icing at all. So a muffin is bread and a cupcake is cake.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"scone\",\"scones\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"rock cake\",\"rock cakes\",\"rock bun\",\"rock buns\"]},\"A scone is a soft dough rolled and cut, baked hot for 10 to 12 minutes, and it should be light enough to break open. A rock cake is a stiff dough with dried fruit dropped in rough lumps, so it bakes into a craggy top - heavier, sweeter, and it keeps for days where a scone does not.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"solicitor\",\"solicitors\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"barrister\",\"barristers\"]},\"A solicitor does the day-to-day work: contracts, letters, a house purchase, the first meeting. A barrister is the one who argues in court, and you reach one through a solicitor. A lawyer is the general word for both.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"hire\",\"hiring\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"rent\",\"renting\"]},\"You hire a thing for hours or days - a van, a carpet cleaner, a hall - and rent a home or a piece of land for months or years. Hire is short and usually about the item, rent is long and usually about the place.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"bank\",\"banks\",\"high street bank\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"building society\",\"building societies\",\"mutual\"]},\"A bank is owned by shareholders; a building society is owned by the people who save with it and borrow from it, which is why its profit goes back out as better rates rather than a dividend. Your money is protected the same either way - £85,000 per person per bank or society under the FSCS - and the card, the ISA and the app work the same. Choose on the rate, not the label.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sale\",\"sales\",\"in the sale\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"offer\",\"offers\",\"on offer\"]},\"An offer is a lower price on one thing, usually for a set time; a sale is a shop cutting prices across the board. Neither word has a legal meaning, so the price on the till is the one that counts - and your right to a refund on something in a sale is exactly the same as outside one.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"envy\",\"envious\",\"jealousy of\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"jealous\",\"jealousy\"]},\"Envy is wanting what someone else has: their house, their job, their holiday. Jealousy is the fear of losing what you have, and it needs a third person - a partner's new friend, a colleague who is close to your boss. So envy looks outwards and jealousy guards something.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"warranty\",\"warranties\",\"extended warranty\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"guarantee\",\"guarantees\",\"manufacturer guarantee\"]},\"A guarantee is the maker's own promise to repair or replace the thing within a set time, usually a year or two and often only if you registered it. A warranty is usually the extra cover a shop sells you. Neither replaces your rights against the retailer: in England and Wales a faulty product can be put right for up to six years, warranty or no warranty.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sprain\",\"sprains\",\"sprained\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"strain\",\"strains\",\"pulled muscle\",\"pulled a muscle\"]},\"A sprain is a stretched or torn ligament - the band joining bone to bone - so it happens at a joint, most often a twisted ankle. A strain is a stretched or torn muscle or tendon in the meat of a leg, back or arm. The first day is the same for both: rest it, ice for 20 minutes every few hours, wrap it, keep it up; see someone if you cannot put weight on it.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"fracture\",\"fractures\",\"fractured\",\"broken bone\",\"broken bones\",\"hairline fracture\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"break\",\"breaks\",\"broken\",\"broke\"]},\"Nothing: a fracture and a break are the same injury, and a doctor saying fracture is not saying it is worse. A hairline or stress fracture is a fine crack, and a greenstick fracture is a bone bent and cracked on one side, which is what children get. What changes the treatment is not the word but where the bone is and whether the ends still line up, so ask about that instead.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"leasehold\",\"leaseholder\",\"leaseholders\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"freehold\",\"freeholder\",\"freeholders\"]},\"Freehold means you own the building and the land under it; leasehold means you own the right to live there for a fixed number of years and someone else owns the building and the ground. A leaseholder pays ground rent and usually a service charge, and the lease gets shorter every year, which is what a buyer and a mortgage lender look at. Most flats are leasehold and most houses freehold.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"flat\",\"flats\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"apartment\",\"apartments\"]},\"Nothing: a flat and an apartment are the same home, and the choice is taste - flat is the everyday British word, apartment the estate agent's and the usual one in America and for a serviced block. A maisonette is the one that differs, being on two floors with its own entrance.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"annual\",\"annuals\",\"annual plant\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"perennial\",\"perennials\",\"perennial plant\"]},\"An annual grows, flowers and dies within one year, so it is sown again every spring; a perennial comes back from the same roots year after year. Annuals flower for months and fill a bed cheaply, perennials cost more and give a few weeks each year, so most beds use both.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"mulch\",\"mulching\",\"mulched\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"compost\",\"composting\",\"composted\"]},\"Compost is rotted organic matter dug into the soil to feed it; mulch is anything spread on top of the soil to hold water and keep weeds down, and it can be compost, bark, manure or gravel. So compost improves the soil and mulch is a blanket: you can mulch with compost, but you do not dig gravel in.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"boil\",\"boils\",\"a boil on\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"cyst\",\"cysts\"]},\"A boil is a deep infection of a hair follicle: tender, hot, and it swells up and comes to a head. A cyst is a closed sac under the skin, usually smooth and painless, holding fluid or keratin, and it does not drain and heal by itself. A boil often needs an antibiotic and to drain; a cyst that keeps filling is cut out. Do not squeeze either.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"lager\",\"lagers\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"ale\",\"ales\",\"bitter\",\"real ale\"]},\"Lager and ale are both beer, brewed with different yeast: lager uses a yeast that works cold at the bottom of the tank, ale a yeast that works warm at the top. Cold and slow gives lager its clean, crisp taste; warm and quick gives ale its fruitiness and its hops. Stout and porter are ales brewed dark, so colour says nothing about which one you have.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"lager\",\"lagers\",\"ale\",\"ales\",\"stout\",\"stouts\",\"porter\",\"pilsner\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"beer\",\"beers\"]},\"Beer is the whole family, and lager and ale are the two branches of it: lager is brewed cold with a bottom yeast, ale warm with a top one. So every lager is a beer and not every beer is a lager - bitter, stout, porter and wheat beer are all ales. If a pub list says \\\"beers\\\" it is offering both.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"rabbit\",\"rabbits\",\"bunny\",\"bunnies\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"hare\",\"hares\"]},\"A hare is much bigger and longer-legged than a rabbit, with long ears tipped black, and it lives above ground in a form - a shallow scrape - rather than a burrow. Hares are born fully furred with their eyes open and are running within hours; rabbits are born blind and bald in a lined nest underground. Hares are also solitary and rabbits live in groups, so a big, loping, lonely one in a field is a hare.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"moped\",\"mopeds\",\"scooter\",\"scooters\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"motorbike\",\"motorbikes\",\"motorcycle\",\"motorcycles\"]},\"A moped is up to 50cc and 28mph, and you can ride one at 16 on a provisional licence after a CBT - that is what the pedals-then-engine history of the name means. A motorbike is anything bigger, from a 125 at 17 to a full licence, and it needs the tests, insurance and a proper helmet. A scooter is a shape rather than a class: most small ones are moped-legal at 50cc.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"heart attack\",\"heart attacks\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"panic attack\",\"panic attacks\",\"anxiety attack\"]},\"A heart attack is a blocked artery: heavy, crushing pressure in the middle of the chest, often spreading to the left arm, the jaw or the back, with sweating, sickness and breathlessness, brought on by effort and lasting more than fifteen minutes. A panic attack peaks within ten minutes: racing heart, tingling hands, dizziness and a fear of dying, usually at rest, and it eases as you breathe slowly. Chest pain that is new, crushing or comes with sweating is a 999 call - do not wait to work out which one it is.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"heart rate\",\"pulse\",\"pulse rate\",\"bpm\",\"beats per minute\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"blood pressure\",\"bp\",\"readings\",\"reading\"]},\"Heart rate is how fast the heart beats, counted in beats a minute: 60 to 100 at rest is normal, and it rises with exercise, caffeine and stress. Blood pressure is how hard the blood pushes on the artery walls, written as two numbers - the top one when the heart squeezes, the bottom one between beats - and around 120/80 is a good reading. A fast pulse and a high pressure are separate things: you can have one without the other.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"pill\",\"pills\",\"tablet\",\"tablets\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"capsule\",\"capsules\"]},\"A tablet is powder pressed into a disc, and it can be split or crushed (unless the packet says otherwise, because some are coated to release slowly). A capsule is a shell - usually gelatine or a vegetable gum - filled with powder, granules or liquid, so it is swallowed whole and opens in the stomach. If swallowing is the problem, ask the pharmacist before crushing: many tablets are not meant to be.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"magpie\",\"magpies\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"crow\",\"crows\",\"carrion crow\",\"rook\",\"rooks\"]},\"A magpie is black and white with a long tail, about 45cm, and it is unmistakable. A crow is all black, bigger than a pigeon and often alone or in a pair, with a heavy bill and a harsh caw; rooks are the ones in noisy flocks with bare grey faces. If it has any white on it, it is not a crow.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"maisonette\",\"maisonettes\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"flat\",\"flats\",\"apartment\",\"apartments\",\"bungalow\"]},\"A maisonette is a flat on two floors with its own front door to the outside, so it has stairs inside and no shared hall. A flat is usually on one level off a shared entrance, and a bungalow is a house with everything on the ground floor. A maisonette feels more like a house and is often leasehold all the same, so check the lease and the service charge.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"mortgage broker\",\"brokers\",\"broker\",\"independent adviser\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"bank\",\"banks\",\"building society\",\"lender\",\"lenders\"]},\"A broker does not lend the money: they compare the deals on the market and apply to a lender for you, and many charge a fee on top of the lender's arrangement fee. Going to a bank directly means one lender's own deals with no broker fee, which is fine if your case is straightforward. A whole-of-market broker earns its fee when your pay is unusual, your deposit is small or your credit file is untidy.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"hp\",\"hire purchase\",\"hp agreement\",\"hp finance\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"pcp\",\"personal contract purchase\",\"pcp finance\",\"pcp deal\"]},\"With hire purchase you pay a deposit and fixed monthly payments, and at the end of the term the car is yours - nothing more to pay. With PCP you pay a smaller deposit and smaller months for a mileage limit, then choose at the end: hand the car back, part-exchange it, or pay a large final payment to keep it. PCP is cheaper per month and costs more over the years, and excess miles are charged at a few pence each, so HP suits keeping a car and PCP suits changing it every three years.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"ukulele\",\"uke\",\"ukuleles\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"guitar\",\"guitars\",\"acoustic guitar\"]},\"A ukulele has four nylon strings, a much smaller body and the tuning G-C-E-A; a guitar has six steel or nylon strings in E-A-D-G-B-E and two and a half octaves more range. The ukulele is the easier first instrument by a wide margin - four strings, soft on the fingers, and most chords need two or three fingers - while a guitar can play bass lines and full chords. A baritone ukulele is the size of a small guitar and is tuned to the guitar's top four strings.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"vegan\",\"vegans\",\"veganism\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"vegetarian\",\"vegetarians\",\"vegetarianism\"]},\"A vegetarian eats no meat or fish but does eat dairy and eggs; a vegan eats nothing that comes from an animal at all, so no milk, cheese, butter, eggs or honey, and no gelatine or leather either. Vegan is the stricter one, so every vegan meal is vegetarian and not the other way round. The one thing to watch on a vegan diet is vitamin B12, which is only in animal food, so it comes from fortified milk and cereals or a supplement.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"therapy\",\"therapist\",\"psychotherapy\",\"talking therapy\",\"cbt\",\"psychologist\",\"psychologists\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"counselling\",\"counseling\",\"counsellor\",\"counselor\"]},\"In Britain the words overlap and both mean talking to a trained person, so the honest difference is the shape of the sessions rather than the label. Counselling is usually the listening kind - six to twelve weekly sessions on one problem, such as a bereavement or a decision - while therapy is often longer and follows a method, CBT being the commonest: homework, thought records and a plan you work through. Ask any of them which body they are accredited with, BACP for counsellors and BABCP for CBT, and whether they are on the NHS talking therapies list, where both are free.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chromebook\",\"chromebooks\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"laptop\",\"laptops\",\"windows laptop\",\"macbook\"]},\"A chromebook runs ChromeOS, which is mostly a browser: it starts in seconds, costs a couple of hundred pounds and gets ten hours on a charge, and most of what it does needs a connection. A laptop runs Windows or macOS, so it can install real programs and play games, and it costs two to four times as much. For browsing, writing and schoolwork a chromebook is enough; for photographs, video editing or games it is not.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"osteopath\",\"osteopaths\",\"osteopathy\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"chiropractor\",\"chiropractors\",\"chiropractic\"]},\"Both treat back and joint pain with their hands and both are regulated - osteopaths by the General Osteopathic Council, chiropractors by the General Chiropractic Council - and neither needs a GP referral. An osteopath works on the whole body with slow stretching and rhythmic pressure, and a chiropractor mostly adjusts the spine, often with the quick movement that cracks. For ordinary low back pain the evidence for both is about the same as for physiotherapy, so pick on the person: a first session is usually 40 to 70 pounds.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"mushroom\",\"mushrooms\",\"field mushroom\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"toadstool\",\"toadstools\"]},\"There is no scientific difference: a toadstool is just the old word for a mushroom somebody thought was poisonous, so the two names tell you nothing about whether one is safe to eat. Only the species does, and some of the deadliest in Britain look like ordinary field mushrooms, so pick by species with a book or an expert and never by the word. If someone has eaten an unknown one, keep the remains and ring 111 or the poisons line rather than wait for symptoms.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"bee\",\"bees\",\"bumblebee\",\"bumblebees\",\"honeybee\",\"honeybees\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"wasp\",\"wasps\",\"yellow jacket\",\"yellowjacket\"]},\"A bee is furry, round and brownish or striped softly, and a honeybee dies after one sting because the sting stays in the skin; a wasp is smooth, bright yellow with black bands and a pinched waist, and it can sting over and over. Bees are after nectar and pollen and leave you alone; wasps hunt insects and in late summer want sugar, which is why they come for your drink. Flick a wasp away rather than swat it, and if a sting brings swelling of the face or trouble breathing, that is 999.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"pandemic\",\"pandemics\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"epidemic\",\"epidemics\"]},\"An epidemic is more cases of an illness than expected in one place or country; a pandemic is the same thing spread across several countries or continents, so every pandemic starts as an epidemic and most epidemics never become one. The third word is endemic: an illness that is always with us at a steady level, like the common cold or flu in winter. Size makes the difference, not how dangerous the germ is.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"latte\",\"lattes\",\"caffe latte\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"cappuccino\",\"cappuccinos\"]},\"Both are espresso and steamed milk, and the difference is the milk: a cappuccino is roughly equal thirds espresso, milk and thick foam in a 150 to 180ml cup, and a latte is mostly milk with a thin layer of foam on top in a 240 to 300ml glass. So a latte is milder and bigger and a cappuccino is foamier and stronger, and a flat white sits between them with two shots and very fine foam.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"midwife\",\"midwives\",\"community midwife\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"health visitor\",\"health visitors\"]},\"A midwife looks after you and the baby through pregnancy, the birth and the first 28 days: the appointments, the birth itself, the checks and the feeding help. A health visitor is a nurse or midwife with extra training who takes over at about ten to fourteen days and stays until the child is five, doing the weighing and development checks, the postnatal depression questions and the advice on sleep, food and behaviour. Both are free on the NHS and you do not need to ask for either - they come to you.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"income tax\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"national insurance\",\"ni contributions\",\"national insurance contributions\"]},\"Income tax is taken from your pay and funds everything the government spends; National Insurance is a separate contribution on your earnings that buys your State Pension and some benefits, so the two lines on a payslip buy different things. NI stops when you reach State Pension age and income tax does not, and only NI needs the qualifying years.\"]}]}")?;
