let __previous_2459 = frame.load(rt, "DIFFERENCES")?; let __rhs_2460 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"moth\",\"moths\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"butterfly\",\"butterflies\"]},\"A butterfly flies by day and rests with its wings folded upright over its back, and its antennae are thin with a club at the tip. A moth mostly flies at night, rests with its wings spread flat or tented, and has feathery or plain antennae - a few, like the hummingbird hawk-moth, fly by day and still read as moths.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"rabbit\",\"rabbits\",\"bunny\",\"bunnies\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"hare\",\"hares\"]},\"A hare is bigger and lankier, with long ears and long back legs, and its young are born furred with their eyes open, in a scrape on the ground, ready to run within hours. A rabbit is smaller and rounder, lives in a burrow in a group, and its young are born blind, bald and helpless. So a leveret sitting still in a field is normal - leave it where it is.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"bee\",\"bees\",\"honeybee\",\"honeybees\",\"bumblebee\",\"bumblebees\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"wasp\",\"wasps\",\"yellow jacket\"]},\"A bee is fuzzy and lives on pollen and nectar, and only defends the nest - a honeybee dies when it stings. A wasp is smooth and bare, with a tight waist and bright yellow bands, and it hunts other insects for its grubs; in late summer, when the grubs are grown, it scavenges anything sweet and stings more, and it can sting again and again.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"wasp\",\"wasps\",\"yellow jacket\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"hornet\",\"hornets\"]},\"A hornet is the biggest of the wasp family - a European hornet is 3 to 3.5 cm - and it is brown with orange bands rather than black and yellow. Its sting is no worse venom for venom than a wasp's, there is simply more of it, and it is far less interested in your picnic: it hunts insects at dusk. Sightings of the Asian hornet should go to the app or the number on the Government's page.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"crow\",\"crows\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"raven\",\"ravens\"]},\"A raven is much bigger - getting on for buzzard size, twice the weight of a carrion crow - with a heavy bill, shaggy throat feathers, a wedge-shaped tail and a deep croaking call. A crow has a fanned tail and a harsh caw, and gathers in flocks in fields and towns, while ravens keep to pairs on moors, cliffs and hills.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"monkey\",\"monkeys\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"ape\",\"apes\"]},\"An ape has no tail, a broad chest and arms built for hanging from branches, and a bigger brain: gibbons, chimps, gorillas, orangs and people. A monkey usually has a tail and runs along a branch on all fours: baboons, macaques, marmosets. So a chimpanzee is an ape and a baboon is a monkey.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"seal\",\"seals\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"sea lion\",\"sea lions\"]},\"A sea lion has small ear flaps you can see, long front flippers it can walk on, and it barks; a true seal has no ear flaps, short front flippers, and it hauls itself along on its belly, and it is mostly silent. So the seal on a British beach is a grey or common seal, one of the true seals.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"rat\",\"rats\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"mouse\",\"mice\"]},\"A rat runs to 20 to 25 cm in the body, with a thick tail as long again, a blunt nose and small ears; a mouse is 7 to 10 cm, with a pointed nose, big ears and a thin tail about as long as its body. Rats travel the same run each night from drains, rubbish and walls; house mice live indoors in cupboards and under the floor.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"hamster\",\"hamsters\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"gerbil\",\"gerbils\"]},\"A hamster is stocky, lives alone and sleeps most of the day, and two adults in one cage will fight. A gerbil is slimmer with a long tufted tail, lives happily in a pair, and is up and about on and off through the day and night, wanting deep bedding to dig in. So a gerbil wants company and a hamster wants a cage of its own.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"hen\",\"hens\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"chicken\",\"chickens\"]},\"A chicken is the bird; a hen is an adult female, a pullet is a young female before she starts laying, and a cockerel is the male. Hens lay without a cockerel - those eggs are simply unfertilised - so a household that wants eggs needs hens only.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"goose\",\"geese\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"duck\",\"ducks\"]},\"A goose is the bigger bird, with a long neck and legs set further back, and it grazes grass; a duck is smaller with a shorter neck, and it dabbles in water for insects and weed. Geese are louder, bolder and better guards, and ducks are calmer and easier in a small garden.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sheep\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"lamb\",\"lambs\"]},\"A lamb is a sheep under about a year old; a hogget is one to two years, and mutton is older than that. Lamb is milder and quicker to cook, and mutton has more fat and flavour and wants a long, slow pot.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"koala\",\"koalas\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"bear\",\"bears\"]},\"A koala is not a bear: it is a marsupial, related to the wombat, that carries its joey in a pouch and lives almost entirely on eucalyptus leaves. A bear is a placental meat-eater, so the two are on different branches of the mammals altogether.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"bison\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"buffalo\",\"buffaloes\",\"water buffalo\"]},\"A bison has a huge shoulder hump, a beard and a shaggy woolly coat, and it lives on the plains of North America and Europe. A buffalo is a different animal - the water buffalo of Asia and the Cape buffalo of Africa - and both carry horns that curve out, with no shoulder hump. The one in the western and on the nickel is a bison.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"centipede\",\"centipedes\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"millipede\",\"millipedes\"]},\"A centipede has one pair of legs to each segment, a flattened body and real speed: it hunts, and the front pair of legs carries venom. A millipede has two pairs to a segment and a round body, is slow, has no venom, and lives on rotting leaves.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"llama\",\"llamas\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"alpaca\",\"alpacas\"]},\"An alpaca is the smaller of the two, with a short blunt face and upright, banana-shaped ears, and it is kept for its fine wool. A llama is taller, with a longer head and long ears that curve back, and it is used as a pack animal and as a guard for a flock. Llamas are more independent and will face a fox; alpacas are easily spooked.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"dolphin\",\"dolphins\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"porpoise\",\"porpoises\"]},\"A dolphin has a long beak, cone-shaped teeth and a curved fin, and it is sociable and noisy. A porpoise is smaller and stouter, with a blunt face, spade-shaped teeth and a small triangular fin, and it is shy and quiet - so the small grey back arcing fast off a British shore, with no show at all, is usually a porpoise.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"hawk\",\"hawks\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"falcon\",\"falcons\"]},\"A hawk is broad-winged with rounded tips and a plain hooked bill, and it hunts from a perch or a long soar: buzzards, sparrowhawks, goshawks. A falcon has long pointed wings and a notch on the beak, and it hunts in fast level flight or a stoop: kestrels, peregrines, hobbies. So the bird hovering over a verge is a kestrel, a falcon, and the one circling on flat wings with a mewing call is a buzzard, a hawk.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sweet potato\",\"sweet potatoes\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"yam\",\"yams\"]},\"Sweet potatoes are the orange- or cream-fleshed roots in most supermarkets; true yams are the big dark roots with bark-like skin sold in African and Caribbean grocers, and they need peeling and a long cook. In America an orange 'yam' is usually a sweet potato under another name, so cook what you bought as you would a sweet potato.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"courgette\",\"courgettes\",\"zucchini\",\"zucchinis\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"cucumber\",\"cucumbers\"]},\"A courgette comes from the marrow family and is cooked: soft edible skin, spongy seedy middle, and it softens in the pan. A cucumber is watery and eaten raw, usually peeled or scored, and it turns to mush if you cook it. Small ones look alike; the taste does not.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"clementine\",\"clementines\",\"satsuma\",\"satsumas\",\"tangerine\",\"tangerines\",\"mandarin\",\"mandarins\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"lemon\",\"lemons\",\"orange\",\"oranges\",\"grapefruit\"]},\"All the easy peelers are mandarins: a satsuma is the earliest, with the loosest skin and usually no pips, a clementine is smaller and sweeter and sometimes has a few, and a tangerine is deeper orange with a stronger taste. Sweet and easy to peel means a satsuma or clementine, so pick one that feels light for its size - and a lemon, an orange or a grapefruit is none of them.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"clementine\",\"clementines\",\"tangerine\",\"tangerines\",\"mandarin\",\"mandarins\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"satsuma\",\"satsumas\"]},\"A satsuma is the loosest-skinned easy peeler and usually has no pips, and it is the earliest of them in the shops. A clementine is smaller and sweeter with a tighter skin, and it sometimes has a few pips. Both are mandarins, so buy whichever feels light for its size.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"latte\",\"lattes\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"flat white\",\"flat whites\"]},\"A latte is a shot of espresso with a lot of steamed milk, around 220ml in a cafe mug, so it is mild and milky. A flat white is the same shot with far less milk, about 130ml, in a smaller cup, so the coffee tastes stronger. If you want the coffee to taste of coffee, order the flat white.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"lease\",\"leases\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"tenancy\",\"tenancies\",\"tenancy agreement\"]},\"In Scotland a lease is what the rest of the UK calls a tenancy: the written agreement that sets the rent and the notice. In England and Wales the usual one is an assured shorthold tenancy, and a lease is the long agreement you buy when you own a flat. So a lease in Scotland is short and a lease in England is long.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"jam\",\"jams\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"jelly\",\"jellies\",\"preserve\",\"preserves\"]},\"In Britain jam has the fruit in it and jelly is the clear set made from strained juice, and in America 'jelly' is that clear set while 'jam' is the British jam. Marmalade is citrus with shreds of peel, and a preserve is the chunky one with whole or large pieces of fruit. So a US recipe that says jelly wants the smooth, clear set.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"griddle\",\"griddles\",\"griddle pan\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"frying pan\",\"frying pans\",\"fry pan\"]},\"A griddle is flat, or ridged, and heavy, with low or no sides: a plate of heat for pancakes, bacon and several chops at once, and fat runs off a ridged one. A frying pan has deep sloping sides, so things can be tossed in it and the fat or sauce stays in.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"slow cooker\",\"slow cookers\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"pressure cooker\",\"pressure cookers\"]},\"A slow cooker cooks on low for six to eight hours and can be left all day; a pressure cooker seals the steam in and does the same work in a third of the time or less, under pressure. Beans, tough cuts and stock are far quicker in the pressure cooker, and a stew you want waiting when you get in is the slow cooker's.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"broil\",\"broils\",\"broiling\",\"broiled\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"grill\",\"grills\",\"grilling\",\"grilled\"]},\"In Britain the grill is the heat from above and a barbecue is over the coals; in America 'broil' is the heat from above and 'grill' is over the coals. So a US recipe that says broil means the grill pan under the element, and where an American says grill, light the barbecue.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"jumper\",\"jumpers\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"sweater\",\"sweaters\"]},\"Nothing: a jumper and a sweater are the same knitted top, jumper being the British word and sweater the American one. A cardigan is the one that opens down the front, and a pullover is any of them you put on over your head.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"trainer\",\"trainers\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"sneaker\",\"sneakers\"]},\"Nothing: a trainer is the British word for a sneaker, and both are the same soft sports shoe. Plimsolls are the flat canvas ones, and 'runners' is what Americans call the sort you run in.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"biscuit\",\"biscuits\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"cookie\",\"cookies\"]},\"In Britain a biscuit is the crisp flat sort - digestives, rich tea - and a cookie is the soft, chunky American-style one. In America both are cookies, and an American biscuit is a soft, scone-like bread eaten with gravy. So a British recipe for cookies wants the chewy kind.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"savings account\",\"savings accounts\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"isa\",\"isas\",\"cash isa\",\"cash isas\"]},\"Interest in a cash ISA is free of tax; interest in an ordinary savings account is taxed once it is past your personal savings allowance - £1,000 a year at basic rate, £500 at higher rate, nothing at additional rate. So if the rates are close the ISA wins, and if the ordinary account pays much more, do the sum.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"loan\",\"loans\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"overdraft\",\"overdrafts\"]},\"An overdraft is borrowing on your current account, meant for days rather than months: it is charged by the day or the month and the bank can withdraw it. A loan is a fixed sum paid back over an agreed term at an agreed rate. So a few days over is an overdraft, and anything over a month or two is usually cheaper as a loan.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tenant\",\"tenants\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"lodger\",\"lodgers\"]},\"A tenant rents a whole home and has a tenancy, so the landlord needs a court order to evict them and the notice the law sets. A lodger lives in the same home as the owner, sharing the kitchen and bathroom, and can be asked to leave on reasonable notice - usually the rent period. So the spare room in your own house holds a lodger, and the flat next door a tenant.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"supervisor\",\"supervisors\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"manager\",\"managers\"]},\"A supervisor runs the shift: what gets done today, by whom, and to what standard. A manager carries the budget, the hiring, the targets and the reviews. Titles vary from one employer to the next, so the tell is who spends the money and who decides the people.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"loft\",\"lofts\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"attic\",\"attics\"]},\"The same space under the roof: a loft is the bare one holding the boxes, and an attic is that space made into a room. In Britain the job is a loft conversion; in America it is an attic room.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"patio\",\"patios\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"deck\",\"decks\",\"decking\"]},\"A patio is paving or concrete laid on the ground; a deck is timber boards on a raised frame. A patio is cheaper, lasts decades with little care and stays cool underfoot; a deck goes down faster on uneven ground, is warmer barefoot and needs treating and cleaning every year or two.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"shrub\",\"shrubs\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"bush\",\"bushes\"]},\"Nothing: a shrub is the gardener's word for a bush, a woody plant with several stems from the base rather than one trunk. If the stems meet the ground in a cluster it is a shrub; a tree has a single trunk.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"statement\",\"statements\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"receipt\",\"receipts\"]},\"A receipt is the proof of one purchase, and it is what a shop asks for if you want a refund or a swap. A bank statement lists everything that went in and out of an account over a month. Keep the receipt for anything you might return, and the statement is for checking what left your account.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cv\",\"cvs\",\"resume\",\"resumes\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"cover letter\",\"covering letter\",\"covering letters\",\"cover letters\"]},\"A CV is the one- or two-page record of what you have done - jobs, dates, qualifications - and it is the same document for every application. A cover letter is the short note written for that one job: why you want it and what you would bring. The CV carries the facts and the letter makes the case.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"psychiatrist\",\"psychiatrists\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"psychologist\",\"psychologists\"]},\"A psychiatrist is a medical doctor who can diagnose mental illness and prescribe medicine; a psychologist is trained in psychology and works with talking therapy and testing, and cannot prescribe. In Britain a GP refers you to a psychiatrist, and you can reach a psychologist through the NHS or privately.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"novella\",\"novellas\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"novel\",\"novels\"]},\"A novel is the long one, usually over 50,000 words; a novella runs from about 17,500 to 40,000, long enough for a chapter of depth and short enough to read in an evening. Under about 17,500 it is a long short story. Publishers are loose about the line; for a reader, judge by whether it takes a sitting.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"autobiography\",\"autobiographies\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"biography\",\"biographies\"]},\"An autobiography is a life written by the person who lived it, and a biography is written by somebody else. A memoir is the autobiography's selective cousin: the part of a life that bears on one theme.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cold sore\",\"cold sores\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"ulcer\",\"ulcers\"]},\"A cold sore is the herpes virus: a cluster of small blisters on a tingle, usually at the edge of the lip, which crusts over in a few days and comes back in the same spot when you are run down. A mouth ulcer is a raw pale patch inside the mouth, on the tongue, cheek or gum - not blistered and not catching - and it usually heals in a week or two. A cold sore is worth a pharmacist's cream in the first day or so; an ulcer that lasts past three weeks is worth showing to a dentist.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"stock cube\",\"stock cubes\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"bouillon cube\",\"bouillon cubes\",\"bouillon\"]},\"Nothing much: bouillon is French for stock, and a bouillon cube is the same cube of salt, yeast extract and flavourings in a different wrapper. Powder, paste and jelly pots do the same job. What matters is the salt - taste before you season - and whether the stock is the point of the dish, because fresh stock beats a cube when it is.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"fridge\",\"fridges\",\"refrigerator\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"freezer\",\"freezers\"]},\"A fridge runs at 0 to 5C, cold enough to slow the bugs that spoil food: milk keeps for days and cooked food for a few. A freezer runs at -18C, where almost nothing grows, so food keeps for months - but freezing does not kill the bugs, it only parks them, so it still has to be cooked properly after it thaws.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tune\",\"tunes\",\"melody\",\"melodies\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"song\",\"songs\"]},\"A tune is the melody on its own, the bit you hum; a song has words and a voice on top of the tune. So an instrumental has a tune but is not a song, and something the words carry - a rap, a hymn sung flat - is still a song.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"shallow fry\",\"shallow frying\",\"shallow-fry\",\"shallow-frying\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"deep fry\",\"deep frying\",\"deep-fry\",\"deep-frying\"]},\"Shallow frying is a centimetre or two of oil in a pan, with the food turned once; deep frying covers the food, so it crisps all over and cooks quickly. Deep frying wants more oil, a thermometer and a lid, and 170 to 190C - too cool and the food drinks the oil, too hot and the outside burns before the middle is done.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"puppy\",\"puppies\",\"pup\",\"pups\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"dog\",\"dogs\"]},\"A puppy is a dog under about a year, and the difference that matters is what it can do: a puppy eats food built for growth, three or four small meals a day, and needs short play and long sleeps. An adult dog eats twice a day and can run for an hour. Big breeds are still growing at 18 months, so a large puppy at a year is still a puppy.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"kitten\",\"kittens\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"cat\",\"cats\"]},\"A kitten is a cat under about a year: it needs kitten food with more protein and fat, several small meals, warmth and company, and everything is still being learned - scratch posts, short gentle play, and one room at a time in a new house. A grown cat wants less food and less fuss, and it sleeps two thirds of the day.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"magpie\",\"magpies\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"crow\",\"crows\",\"raven\",\"ravens\"]},\"A magpie is a corvid the size of a small crow, black and white with a long wedge of a tail; a crow is all black, bigger, and gathers in flocks in fields. Both are in the crow family, with the jay, the jackdaw and the rook.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"syrup\",\"syrups\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"sauce\",\"sauces\"]},\"A syrup is sugar dissolved in water - golden, maple, treacle - thin and pourable; a sauce is thickened to coat, with flour, cornflour, egg or cream, and it may not be sweet at all. A syrup is poured over and soaks in; a sauce sits on top.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"contract\",\"contracts\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"agreement\",\"agreements\"]},\"An agreement is any two people saying yes to the same thing; a contract is an agreement the law will enforce, which needs an offer, an acceptance and something of value each way - and no signature at all, since a yes by email or a deposit paid can be enough. So every contract is an agreement, and most agreements are not contracts.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"credit score\",\"credit scores\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"credit report\",\"credit reports\",\"credit file\",\"credit files\"]},\"The report is the record: every account, payment and search in your name, kept by Experian, Equifax and TransUnion. The score is a number one of those agencies works out from the report. So you fix the report - correct the errors, register to vote, pay on time, keep balances low - and the score follows.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"meeting\",\"meetings\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"catch up\",\"catch-up\",\"catchup\",\"catch ups\"]},\"A meeting has an agenda and a decision at the end; a catch-up is a short, informal check-in with no decision to make, usually one to one. Call a meeting when something has to be agreed and a catch-up when you only need to stay in touch - and say which it is in the invitation.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"hedge\",\"hedges\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"fence\",\"fences\"]},\"A hedge is living, so it wants clipping once or twice a year and it dies if it is not watered in a drought; a fence is built, wants treating every few years and will need replacing in 15 to 20. A hedge gives birds cover and slows the wind; a fence goes up in a weekend, costs less and takes up no ground.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"squirrel\",\"squirrels\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"chipmunk\",\"chipmunks\"]},\"A chipmunk is much smaller - about 15 cm in the body, with a short tail - and it has stripes down its face and back and lives on the ground in a burrow in North America. A squirrel is bigger, with a long bushy tail and no face stripes, and it climbs. So the striped thing in a British garden is a grey squirrel in good light, not a chipmunk.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"lizard\",\"lizards\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"gecko\",\"geckos\"]},\"A gecko is one family of lizard: soft skin with tiny scales, no eyelids on most kinds (they lick the eye clean), toe pads that grip glass, and a chirp. The lizard in a British garden is usually a common lizard or a slow worm - dry scales, eyelids, and no voice at all.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"career\",\"careers\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"job\",\"jobs\"]},\"A job is what you are paid to do now, with a contract and a wage; a career is the run of them and the direction - the skills, the reputation, the next step. So changing jobs can be no change of career at all, and a career change often starts with a pay cut.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"bungalow\",\"bungalows\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"house\",\"houses\"]},\"A bungalow is a house of one storey, so there are no stairs; house covers any of them. In Britain the word usually means a single-storey home with its own front door, and it is priced and built differently: easier to live in with a wheelchair, and with more roof to extend into.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"nurse\",\"nurses\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"carer\",\"carers\"]},\"A nurse is registered with the nursing council and does the clinical work - medicines, wounds, observations - in a hospital, surgery or care home. A carer helps with daily living: washing, dressing, meals and company, and needs no registration, whether it is a paid care worker or a relative doing it unpaid. So a health decision is the nurse's, and the help through the day is the carer's.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"boiler\",\"boilers\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"furnace\",\"furnaces\"]},\"A boiler heats water and sends it round the radiators and the taps. A furnace heats air and blows it through ducts, which is the usual American heating; an old British back boiler is a boiler behind a fire. So a boiler has a flow temperature that matters and a furnace has a fan - the same job done through a different pipe.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sprain\",\"sprains\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"break\",\"breaks\",\"fracture\",\"fractures\"]},\"A sprain is a stretched or torn ligament at a joint, and a break is bone, which hurts over the bone itself and swells. You cannot tell them apart by how much it hurts, so the test is what you can do: if you cannot put weight on it, it is bent oddly, or you cannot use the limb, get it looked at the same day and let them X-ray it.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"pond\",\"ponds\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"pool\",\"pools\",\"swimming pool\",\"swimming pools\"]},\"A pond is a small still body of water, in a garden or a field, with plants, mud and wildlife, and nothing keeps it clean but the plants and the balance. A pool is built and filtered for swimming, so it needs a pump, chemicals and a cover. So a pond wants the shallow edge and the frogs, and a pool wants the filter.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"rabbit\",\"rabbits\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"guinea pig\",\"guinea pigs\",\"cavy\",\"cavies\"]},\"A guinea pig is the smaller, rounder one, with no tail and short legs, and it cannot make its own vitamin C, so it needs it in the food or in a supplement. A rabbit is bigger, with long ears and back legs, and it needs a run it can stand up in and dig. Guinea pigs want company of their own kind; a rabbit is strong enough to hurt one by accident, so a pair of rabbits or a pair of guinea pigs, not one of each.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"fine\",\"fines\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"penalty\",\"penalties\"]},\"A fine is money a court or a council orders you to pay for breaking a rule. A penalty is the wider word: it is any punishment or extra charge - a penalty fare on the train, a penalty charge notice on the car, a late-payment penalty on a bill. So every fine is a penalty, and most penalties are not fines.\"]}]}")?; let __updated_2461 = pyrt::ops::inplace(rt, "+", &__previous_2459, &__rhs_2460)?; frame.store("DIFFERENCES", __updated_2461)?;
